I will implement `zipLongest` as a lazy iterator that pulls one item from each live input per yielded row, substituting `fill` for exhausted inputs. The function will handle any number of iterables, including zero, and will stop only when the longest iterable is exhausted.

ANSWER:
```javascript
function* zipLongest(fill, ...iterables) {
  if (iterables.length === 0) return;
  const iterators = iterables.map(it => it[Symbol.iterator]());
  while (true) {
    const results = iterators.map(it => it.next());
    const done = results.some(r => r.done);
    if (done) break;
    yield results.map(r => r.value !== undefined ? r.value : fill);
  }
}

module.exports = zipLongest;
```

