hsh-008.text:
I will parse each line of access.log, extract the path and status code, and count only those with status 200. I'll store the counts in an associative array, then output the results sorted by count descending and path ascending, writing each `path count` pair to summary.txt. Paths with no 200 responses will be omitted.

ANSWER:
awk -v OFS=' ' '
  $3 == "200" {
    count[$4]++
  }
  END {
    n = asorti(count, paths)
    for (i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      p = paths[i]
      printf "%s %d\n", p, count[p]
    } | "sort -k2,2nr -k1,1" > summary.txt
  }
' access.log

