hgit-006.text:
The approach is to use `git rev-list` to list all commits reachable from the current branch (`HEAD`) and exclude those reachable from the first commit (the root). The `git rev-list HEAD ^$(git rev-list --max-parents=0 HEAD)` command lists commits that are on the current branch but not reachable from the root. Counting these with `wc -l` gives the desired number. Edge cases include repositories with a single commit (where the count is 0) or no commits (where the count is also 0).

ANSWER:
export OUT=$(git rev-list HEAD ^$(git rev-list --max-parents=0 HEAD) | wc -l)

